description:
In repos/goal-host-vessel/src/index.ts, penaliseHollowTemplate must report the beta it actually applied, not the beta it attempted. Make three changes, all inside that one function.

CHANGE 1 — replace this exact line:
async function penaliseHollowTemplate(activityId: string, reason: string, goalText?: string): Promise<{ templateId: string; dAlpha: number; dBeta: number }> {

with this exact line:
async function penaliseHollowTemplate(activityId: string, reason: string, goalText?: string): Promise<{ templateId: string; dAlpha: number; dBeta: number }> { let _betaApplied = false;

CHANGE 2 — replace this exact line:
    if (!res.ok) console.warn(`[goal-host-vessel] beta-penalty REJECTED (${res.status}) for '${activityId}' — no posterior row exists for this pick; penalty not applied`);

with this exact line:
    if (!res.ok) console.warn(`[goal-host-vessel] beta-penalty REJECTED (${res.status}) for '${activityId}' — no posterior row exists for this pick; penalty not applied`); else _betaApplied = true;

CHANGE 3 — replace this exact line:
  return { templateId: activityId, dAlpha: 0, dBeta: 2 };

with this exact line:
  return { templateId: activityId, dAlpha: 0, dBeta: _betaApplied ? 2 : 0 };

Why: the caller pushes this return value into learningSink.alphaBetaDelta, which is what the dispatch record shows an operator as the learning consequence of the goal. The function currently returns dBeta 2 unconditionally, including on the path where it has just logged that the penalty was NOT applied. Measured in one 20-minute window on the live spoke, three penalties were rejected with 404 for the arms patch_with_tools and feature_compose because no posterior row exists for those picks, and every one of them was still reported as a delta of 2.

This is the same defect the alpha site already fixed and documented in the comment beginning "Report what HAPPENED, not what was attempted" — that line once fired unconditionally, so a credit that was rejected or lost still read as alpha-credited. The alpha path was corrected to report dAlpha only when it is greater than zero. The beta path was never given the same treatment, so it still asserts a penalty the store refused.

